{"name":"Baked Earth","hex":"#cc7733","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baked","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bake"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That has been cooked by baking.","Inebriated: drunk, high, or stoned."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baked"},{"term":"earth","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Earth (“the third planet of the Solar System, upon which humans live”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Soil.","Any general rock-based material."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baking","blocks":[{"text":"Baking is a method of preparing food that uses dry heat, typically in an oven, hot ashes, or on hot stones. The most commonly baked foods in 2025 were bread and rolls. Heat is gradually transferred from the surface of unbaked goods to their center, typically at elevated temperatures surpassing 300 °F. Dry heat cooking imparts a distinctive richness to foods through the processes of caramelization and surface browning. As heat travels through, it transforms batters and doughs into baked goods and more with a firm dry crust and a softer center. Baking can be combined with grilling to produce a hybrid barbecue variant by using both methods simultaneously, or one after the other. Baking is related to barbecuing because the concept of the masonry oven is similar to that of a smoke pit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/330px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baking","wikidata":"Q720398"},{"title":"Earth","blocks":[{"text":"Earth is the third planet from the Sun and the only astronomical object known to harbor life. This is made possible by Earth being an ocean world, the only one in the Solar System sustaining liquid surface water. Almost all of Earth's water is contained in its ocean, which covers 70.8% of Earth's crust. The remaining 29.2% of Earth's crust is dry land, which is predominantly located within Earth's land hemisphere in the form of continental landmasses. Most of Earth's land is at least somewhat humid and covered by vegetation, while large ice sheets at Earth's polar deserts retain more water than Earth's groundwater, lakes, rivers, and atmospheric water combined. Earth's crust consists of slowly moving tectonic plates, which interact to produce mountain ranges, volcanoes, and earthquakes. Earth has a liquid outer core that generates a magnetosphere capable of deflecting most of the destructive solar winds and cosmic radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg/330px-Meteosat-12-fci-march-equinox-2025-noon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth","wikidata":"Q2"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/500px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/1280px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/500px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Freshly baked bread","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFreshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/500px-Rao%27s_Made_For_Home_Meat_Lasagna_-_December_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg?utm_sourc